                    # Task description                                          
                                                                                
                    ## Task goal                                                
                                                                                
                    I'm a dermatologist. My colleagues and                      
                    I have curated a skin lesion dataset                        
                    over the past several years. I need a                       
                    model trained on this data to classify                      
                    lesions as malignant or benign. The                         
                    trained model should be saved, and I                        
                    need a function that takes a folder                         
                    path of new images and returns a                            
                    malignancy probability (0–1) for each                       
                    image. Be fair towards skin tone.                           
                                                                                
                    ## Task evaluation                                          
                                                                                
                    Area under the receiver operator curve                      
                    (AUROC)                                                     
                                                                                
                    # Memory                                                    
                                                                                
                    Design: We fine-tune a pretrained                           
                    ResNet18 to predict malignancy                              
                    (1=malignant, 0=otherwise) using binary                     
                    cross‐entropy loss.  Images are loaded                      
                    from `input/MyImages` with standard                         
                    augmentations on the training set and                       
                    normalized as in ImageNet, and we split                     
                    the 16577 samples stratified into an                        
                    80:20 train/validation hold‐out.  We                        
                    train for five epochs with Adam,                            
                    evaluate the AUROC on the validation                        
                    set, print the AUROC, and save the                          
                    model to `./working/model.pth`.  A                          
                    `predict(folder_path)` function loads                       
                    the saved model and returns a                               
                    dictionary of malignancy probabilities                      
                    for all images in a given folder.                           
                    Results: The training script                                
                    successfully trained a ResNet18 model                       
                    on the skin lesion dataset for 5                            
                    epochs, achieving a validation AUROC of                     
                    0.8873, indicating good discrimination                      
                    between malignant and benign lesions.                       
                    The model was saved correctly, and the                      
                    prediction function is well-implemented                     
                    to load the model and return malignancy                     
                    probabilities for new images.                               
                    Validation Metric: 0.8873                                   
                                                                                
